  "question": {
    "text": "The pressure of a moist gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>. The volume of the container is doubled at the same temperature. The new pressure of the moist gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> atm. (Nearest integer)<br />(Given: The vapour pressure of water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Dalton&#39;s Law states that the total pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> of moist air is the sum of partial pressures of dry air <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and water vapor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub></math>:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub></math>. Only the absolute pressure is the state parameter of moist air.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math></p><p>As volume is doubled, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub></mfenced><mrow><mi>new</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math></p><p>New Total Pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}